    "reason": "[ev-628f9c0eccb2] and [ev-4c2676e4665a] say support was removed only for ZooKeeper-based clusters and ZooKeeper-to-KRaft migration, and that clusters must be using KRaft before the upgrade. That means KRaft clusters are not exposed. The proposed any[] flags every environment that uses Kafka v1beta2 or v1beta1, which includes all KRaft clusters, so it is far too broad. Neither the changelog nor the upgrade notes name the field or setting that marks a cluster as ZooKeeper-based. So the corrected condition requires a Kafka resource and leaves the ZooKeeper-mode test as an evidence gap instead of using spec.zookeeper, which no evidence names.",
